7nbdJL5nDW-wEkfWFcCp0VqrSE6kq6N3zhBh0ou0JOkqvUh4v4WvO0rQim_1dV0dCgc4mG_ogcGhte0t9Dfc622NceptwwJ4yCBrVJFL5JBFzvaNj1lU_YzhJCP7K2lMhyTys3bgu4316PBVI1CQltkQ-HK6WAgu4lq3Uo6xkenxTSg_e7YhGlRiMw9gnRXbZSW5zaKzj7i1tbMh3GGHcA5AyHkAEjZ3LE1y2xqXBGej7XcHASnIYMJA-Xe9ATxHNq969HtoUsbfZ30DfByYdJsxHUfkSbL6YNGkObTZAgkRIO2_DXydJUlDdgToLUl7JysvkW8p6xfhwELrTgiVSpmhMV6RzC1ABPzvkb505rkrHJQ_VMW0vYbdsQcJ-KPOD1upQs3KrG4SFZNj-PMVsw7ztWQG0evprnPC6LOSW_OCne_maUPOWtFQNBPzjOJGl7sN-n24gN-eepUuV7AlTJAVi6xO7jhwfR5JF6MP3UFgjXQvJ-nXEnmX0hX-mmXlCLb00Dg1wjbMra8_ezacY7x_G8fFIrH1fZVateyE1_cu0-tTi0ZScKpIyirJMvMGPqYKEs4q-1r5u0TlczWA0HxsxrV2PaySgitQJ1hjx8e22xV0VjVqCW_iwSv21OE6bC8QmM8-LmqSUFg8WznHHL_dtsru8RJs5-tY-Zav1rmWGbR1uXPofVcIfPi0NjqnIteali6-ftmU5SyxXUlDhRr4At8w=="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_09727e22ce4e60ca016ae4a4a0f60481919a94ae826ac70cd5","call_id":"call_6ddc1e211a6845a49e1e92945bba6347","name":"record_author_checks","arguments":"{\"candidate\":9,\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"original_context_note\":\"Compared spec.full_target literally with target-selection.json/full_target and mathematically with problem.md:16-41: arbitrary prime p, arbitrary characteristic-p field K, integer 0<=lambda<p, the specified complex module and highest vector, and an arbitrary admissible lattice are all retained. H001-H004 retain all original givens and their locations; no original H node is unused. Within H002, the irreducible/highest-weight classification is retained even though the calculation only needs its dimension, the displayed commutators, and H003. There is no minimal-lattice or algebraic-closure assumption. D001-D006 preserve n, the divided-power vectors and enveloping-algebra divided powers; D006 carefully distinguishes abstract Chevalley generators from their represented operators. D007-D011 preserve localization, arbitrary-lattice coordinates and the common coefficient module: M_R is initially the R-span image, and R002 proves the required tensor embedding, rather than assuming it. D009 has the proved N001 basis guard, present directly at every relevant inference. R-related definitions have H001 as guard. D012 is precisely the original tensor product. D013/D015 give the original abstract integral Chevalley algebra, not its potentially nonfaithful image on V; the displayed integer matrix model and R006/S004 establish the bracket/action identification, including lambda=0 and characteristic 2. D014 only extends genuinely lattice-preserving operators; R002 supplies preservation before reduction is used. D016 is the usual prime field under H001. The six selected native sources M001-M006 were actually probed in the pinned checkout and their complete signatures compared with their statements: algebra/module structures in M001/M003, finite/free factors and strong rank condition in M002, the finite basis and strong rank condition in M004, and all numerical premises in M005/M006 are present. The corresponding native source contexts were read, including the three IsLocalizedModule clauses. Humphreys is provenance of the frozen exercise, not an imported proof theorem; there is no selected literature E or inaccessible-primary assumption. The graph has one producer for each N/P, only H/M roots, and all six M and five N lie in P's AND closure. The six inference units preserve all five supplied phases, splitting the common-coordinate module and its rank/generator argument into R003 and R004. No supplied core calculation or intermediate argument was omitted. This is my same-author mathematical inspection, not independent Audit A; structural validity alone is not being called mathematical acceptance.\",\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N001 against R001/S001-S003. The export includes positive n and interval cardinality, the basis and e_0=v, both unrestricted characteristic-zero induction formulas, vanishing beyond lambda, all boundary x,y,h matrices, and both divided-power formulas with the zero cases and integer coefficients. Consumers need no unexported eigenvector or termination fact. The factorial normalization and the descending product at i=0 agree with the original.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N002 against R002/S001-S003. The scalar s in the tensor multiplication map is explicitly in R, while r denotes the nonnegative divided-power index. The export contains injectivity/image, rank n and complex spanning, preservation on both M and M_R, all three projector identities, the binomial unit, and the exact matrix-unit composition. Thus later nodes have the complete representation and preservation claims, not merely a reference to the original equation.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N003 against R003/S001-S002. Every coordinate module is identified with the globally defined J using e_0=v. Finite generation and nonzeroness are proved, and the exported isomorphism specifies both summation and inverse coordinates. These are exactly the maps needed for tensoring in R004; no assertion of rank one has been slipped into this output.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N004 against R004/S001-S005. Tensor multiplication is proved injective via localization fractions, not inferred merely from containment in C. The n=n*r0 computation yields rational rank one before choosing generator coordinates. The minimum-valuation argument proves both containments J=Rb and b!=0, and the coordinate decomposition plus complex independence proves the full R-basis assertion. The generator is existentially exported, not a global unguarded choice.\"},{\"id\":\"N005\",\"note\":\"Checked /graph/propositions/@N005 against R005/S001-S003. The ring map, tensor and quotient scalar identifications and their indicated maps are proved. A single compatible nonzero lattice scalar b supplies the beta basis and the matrix-unit family. The x,y,h matrices, invertible factorial range, exact four-factor matrix-unit formula and invariance implication are all exported. The nonzero binomial coefficient in K follows by mapping the R-unit, not by any reduction-of-weights argument. The n>0 clause supplies nonzeroness for the final consumer.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"Checked spec.conclusion and /graph/propositions/@P against R006/S001-S004. The proof quantifies an arbitrary K-subspace, closes the zero/nonzero cases, obtains all basis vectors from a nonzero coordinate using matrix units, and discharges the invariance assumption. Nonzeroness is separately supplied by dim_K=n>0. The abstract Chevalley algebra action is identified explicitly, rather than replacing L(K) by an operator-image quotient. Both lambda=0 and p=2 and arbitrary nonclosed K remain covered.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual R001 packet. S001 uses H001 for the nonnegative interval/positive n, H002 for dimension and the three commutators, and H003 for the induction bases. The simultaneous h/x step has coefficient t(lambda-t+1)+lambda-2t=(t+1)(lambda-t); its temporary induction premise L1 is discharged. S002 derives nonvanishing by the exact i! descending product and H003, isolates every coefficient by a polynomial in h over C, discharges relation L2, and uses the dimension count to obtain a basis. Coefficient comparison at eigenvalue -lambda-2 then proves termination. S003 iterates the displayed matrices and supplies the binomial identification and both out-of-range zero cases. No modular weight separation or absent H004 is used. Ordinary finite-dimensional basis counting is a routine linear-algebra step; the substantive characteristic-zero computation is displayed, not imported.\",\"source_application_check\":\"R001/S003 applies M006 twice with (a,t)=(lambda-i+r,r) and (i+r,r). In the first valid range a-r=lambda-i>=0, and in the second a-r=i>=0; all quantities are natural under the interval restrictions, so t<=a. Its delivered equality binom(a,r)r!(a-r)!=a! gives the desired products by cancelling nonzero complex factorials. These are the exact native hypotheses and no primality premise is falsely attributed to M006.\",\"declaration_check\":\"D001-D005 supply n,I,e,X,Y with full index ranges. The induction index t is local to S001. The arbitrary complex coefficient family a and arbitrary index j are explicitly declared for the independence subargument in S002 and do not escape it. Indices in sums/products and the universally stated formulas are expression-bound. F001/F002 use their own alpha-renamed binders, with no local t leaking into another paragraph. No basis or nonzero vector is assumed by defining e.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual R002 packet. H004 and N001 ground the simultaneous integer/complex basis existence in S001; F001 precedes its witness m in S002. Base change and complex independence establish the tensor embedding, rank and spanning. H004 supplies X/Y stability and H002 gives h=xy-yx, so all reduction guards are established. S003 checks each projector on the N001 basis, including inputs below and above j. H001 gives lambda<p and primality, so the factorial product is p-free; M006 then proves the binomial unit. Composition in the displayed order yields all E_ij, and F002 supplies preservation. Every listed input has an actual role; no choice of a minimal lattice appears.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M004 at S001 is over C and the complex basis from H004; finite dimension from N001 (also H002) makes that basis finite, and C satisfies the strong rank condition. M001 at S002 is A=Z, B=R, T=M, d=m, with the integer basis from F001; R's inclusion algebra structure is valid by the displayed prime-denominator ring check. M006 at S003 has a=lambda, t=j, both natural with j<=lambda from I. The exact factorial identity is used before dividing in R, not an unproved binomial-unit theorem.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The witness m is introduced at S002 only after the F001 existence statement. Its coordinates lie in M and are also regarded in V through the original subgroup inclusion; the two scalar structures are distinguished. E is introduced globally only under N001, which is a direct input here; Pi's nonnegative index is guarded by H001. Scalar s in the exported tensor map is distinct from the divided-power index r. D006 refers to abstract enveloping-algebra elements, whereas X/Y in the proof are their represented endomorphisms.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual R003 packet. N001 gives the genuine basis and e_0=v; H001 ensures 0 is an available index and the localization ring guard. N002 supplies all matrix-unit preservation and finite freeness/spanning. S001 proves every inclusion J_j subset J_i and its reverse and constructs both inverse maps by projections and summation. S002 gives a finite generating list explicitly as coordinate images of a finite basis, and derives nonzeroness from complex spanning of a positive-dimensional space. This uses only the input statements and elementary linearity; there is no reliance on N002's producer body and no premature claim that J is rank one.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No M/E input is used in this inference. The finite-generation image claim is directly established by applying an R-linear coordinate map to the finite basis from N002. The direct-sum claim is proved by the displayed spanning and uniqueness argument, rather than cited as external structure.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The local family J_i is explicitly defined in S001, lives through S002, and is separate from the globally defined J. The indices in the module-inclusion comparisons and coordinate formulas are universally or expression-bound. All uses of E have direct N001 as their construction guard. No generator of J or arbitrary-lattice basis is chosen without grounds.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual R004 packet including S001-S005 and all source applications. N003 gives finite generation, nonzeroness and both coordinate maps. S001 establishes Q as the scalar localization of R at its nonzero elements and uses M003 to reduce tensors to single fractions; zero image then forces a zero numerator. S002 uses N002's free rank n and N001's interval cardinality. S003 constructs mutually inverse tensor-coordinate maps on pure tensors and elementary tuples before the dimension calculation; finite generation of T is already F001. The resulting n=n*r0 and n>0 give r0=1, so J lies on a rational line for a proved reason. S004 discharges the temporary nonzero-rational assumption L1 after the numerator/denominator factor extraction. S005's finite tuple is nonempty because N003 says J!=0; the minimum exponent produces a scalar with both J subset Rb0 and Rb0 subset J. In particular a minimum generator is a unit multiple of b0, proving membership b0 in J. All tensor/rank tools are explicit inputs; ordinary vector-space freeness and finite basis transport are routine background, not an alternative project lemma.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M003 is applied with A=R, B=Q, S=R\\\\{0}, and T=J or M_R. R is an embedded domain by H001/D007, fractions of integers give every rational, nonzero denominators become units, and injectivity supplies the scalar equality criterion. The map's surjectivity clause yields precisely the single-fraction representation used. M001 at S002 base-changes the actual N002 R-basis to Q. M004 then counts that basis; its repeated S003 use counts a product-space basis and its image under the displayed isomorphism. M002 at S003 has finite index I and constant factor T, finite from F001 and free as a Q-vector space; Q has the strong rank condition. M005 at S004 is used on abs(num(q0)) and den(q0), both nonzero under L1; H001 proves p!=1. No prime hypothesis omitted from M005 exists natively, and its two extracted pairs give exactly q0=p^d0 u0 with a unit of R.\",\"declaration_check\":\"T,U and multiplication mu are explicit tensor constructions, with U used only through S003. The basis m is grounded in N002/N001. The coordinate family coord is the inverse-coordinate map exported by N003, not remembered from its producer. q0 and the M005 witness pairs alpha0,A0 and beta0,B0, followed by the definitions d0,u0, are confined to S004 and discharged into F004. In S005 a0 and g come from N003, qg from F003, and compatible exponent/unit pairs from F004. The finite-minimum construction nu_min has a nonempty finite tuple as its guard. b0 is explicitly defined by p^nu_min a0, proved nonzero and in J, and only existentially exported.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual R005 packet. H001 proves denominator and factorial invertibility in K, not algebraic closure. S001 constructs rho and checks it on fractions, gives explicit inverse balanced tensor maps, and checks quotient-representative independence using pK=0. The identification R/pR=F_p follows by reduction of a denominator inverse and the pR kernel. The b0 choice is exactly the existential basis scalar from N004. S002 transfers that R-basis using M001 and tensor-factor exchange, counts it with M004, and transports all N001 matrices; N002 explicitly supplies the needed lattice preservation. S003 first uses r! X_r=x^r as an integer-linear map equality, and only then inverts r! in K. It tensors N002's E identity on M_R, not on M, which avoids falsely requiring every E_ij to preserve M. Its left side is the beta matrix unit; the binomial denominator remains nonzero because rho maps its R-inverse. The W0 invariance implication is introduced and discharged as L1 inside S003.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M001 at S002 has A=R, B=K via rho from F001, T=M_R and the particular N004 basis b0 e_i. It gives a basis in K tensor_R M_R with values 1 tensor b0 e_i; the explicitly described exchange and F001's isomorphism deliver the beta vectors in V(K). M004 applies to this actual K-basis and finite I; K is a field and hence has the strong rank condition. The exact source conclusions are bridged to the opposite tensor order and original tensor product, rather than merely identifying differently ordered products by name.\",\"declaration_check\":\"b0 is a witness of N004 and remains in scope throughout. rho is defined only after its denominators are proved nonzero. beta is introduced in S002 from the already proved isomorphism F001, and F is defined in S003 only after F002 supplies a basis. F001 now exports the actual forward and inverse formulas with statement-bound variables, not a pointer to its proof text. W0 is arbitrary and its invariance assumption is discharged. F_p is explicitly D016 with H001 guard. All uses of complex E have N001 as a direct input and are carefully distinct from the reduced family F.\"},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual final R006 packet. Its only proof premises are H001,H002,N001,N002,N005. S001 fixes W and the N005 basis, introduces invariance L1, and splits the exhaustive zero/nonzero alternatives; L2 is confined to the nonzero branch. S002 uses F001's nonzero-vector existence, defines coordinates using the supplied basis, and proves the existence F003 of a nonzero coefficient before j is chosen. S003 applies the defined matrix unit to w, obtains c_j beta_i, and divides by the nonzero field element; all basis vectors then lie in W. L2 and L1 are discharged to the full implication F002, and S004 universally quantifies W. N005 supplies nonzeroness separately. H002 and N002 give the bracket/action identification for the abstract integral algebra in D015 and its scalar extension; no faithful-representation premise is used. H001 and N001 are used for the endpoint discussion and the distinction between characteristic-zero and reduced weights. The proof never imports a producer's unstated facts.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No M/E theorem is directly applied in R006. N005 is used exactly as its exported existence/basis/matrix-unit/invariance statement. N002 supplies operator preservation, and H002 supplies the commutator relations needed for the displayed finite bracket calculation. The identification of invariant subspaces with L(K)-submodules follows from the three explicitly defined abstract generators spanning L(K), not from a theorem about an operator-image algebra.\",\"declaration_check\":\"beta is an existential witness from N005, F is its explicitly defined matrix-unit family, and W is arbitrary. The witness w is chosen only after F001; c is its coordinate family. The index j is chosen in S003 only after S002's F003 existence statement. w,c,j remain branch-local and do not appear in F002 or P. The scopes labelled R006/S002 for w,c and j have their precise inclusive start/end fields S002-S003 or S003-S003 and correspond to the nonzero branch, which is closed at S003. The t in S004 is universally bound in the action formula for L_Z, and the final conclusion is independent of all private basis/vector choices.\"}] }","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assumption_check","source_application_check","declaration_check"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["candidate","readiness","open_issues","original_context_note","output_notes","inference_notes"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"8c3f3f59-b623-4a10-b9e9-a1c5760f53ab","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"high"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":193262,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3840,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4430,"output_tokens